👨‍💻 Day 4 Real-Life Style Tasks
✅ 1. Diary App (File Writer)

Create a program where the user can type a diary entry.

Save the entry to a file called diary.txt

Each entry should be stored with the date and time

Example:

[2025-08-18 14:35]
Today I started learning file handling in Python!

✅ 2. Notes Reader

Make a program that:

Opens diary.txt

Displays all entries

If the file doesn’t exist, print "No diary entries yet." (use try-except)

✅ 3. Contact Book

Create a contact manager using a text file:

Let the user add new contacts (name, phone, email)

Save them in contacts.txt (one contact per line)

Add a function to search by name and display the result

Example entry in file:

Chloe, 08123456789, chloe@email.com

✅ 4. Word Counter (File Analyzer)

Ask the user for a filename

Open the file and count:

Total words

Total lines

Most common word (bonus)

If the file doesn’t exist, print "File not found."

✅ 5. Error Logger

Create a function that asks the user for a number

Try to divide 100 by that number

If the user enters 0 or something invalid, catch the error

Write the error message into errors.log with a timestamp

⚡ Bonus Challenge: Student Records Database

Create a file students.txt

Each student’s record = Name, Age, Score

Add options:

Add student

View all students

Search student by name

Delete a student (rewrite the file without that record)

